  "narrative": {
    "intro": "S Oil has $513M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date, across 19 awards and an average award size of $27M. Obligations are down 17.7% year over year for the current fiscal-year-to-date period. Obligations rose from $340M in FY21 to a peak of $635M in FY24, then eased to $624M in FY25 and to $513M in FY26. The obligation pattern shows growth through FY24 followed by two years of decline. The count of 19 awards and the $27M average award size signal a portfolio concentrated in large awards rather than many small buys. Current-year totals are partial, so FY2026 to date represents an incomplete year of activity. Review of award timing and expiration schedules will matter because large awards can shift obligations materially within a fiscal year. Contracting officers and program managers should watch award pacing and renewal windows to understand whether the recent declines continue or reverse later in FY2026.",
